:[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,2679,400,69,2075,8,284,760,18,87,481,220,16,91,4779,12564,678,2750,315,400,87,3,369,892,400,69,955,2075,593,284,856,2418,220,11252,678,279,9904,11,18663,553,76602,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nIf $f(x) = |3x - 1|,$ compute all values of $x$ for which $f(f(x)) = x.$  Enter all the solutions, separated by commas.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"a13f46ba47ca4f75ce19afd174e31f6d29b257312f8e3f277c593bf8b3b6b1e4"},"seconds":21.61176037788391,"seed":597799765475051958,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we need to find all values of \\( x \\) such that \\( f(f(x)) = x \\) where \\( f(x) = |3x - 1| \\). Let's proceed step by step.\n\nFirst, we need to express \\( f(f(x)) \\) in terms of \\( x \\). Since \\( f(x) = |3x - 1| \\), we have:\n\\[ f(f(x)) = f(|3x - 1|) = |3|3x - 1| - 1|. \\]\n\nWe need to solve the equation:\n\\[ |3|3x - 1| - 1| = x. \\]\n\nTo do this, we need to consider the cases for the expression inside the absolute value. Let's break it down into cases based on the value of \\( 3x - 1 \\).\n\n### Case 1: \\( 3x - 1 \\geq 0 \\) (i.e., \\( x \\geq \\frac{1}{3} \\))\nIn this case, \\( |3x - 1| = 3x - 1 \\), so:\n\\[ f(f(x)) = |3(3x - 1) - 1| = |9x - 3 - 1| = |9x - 4|. \\]\nWe need to solve:\n\\[ |9x - 4| = x. \\]\nThis gives us two sub-cases:\n1. \\( 9x - 4 = x \\)\n2. \\( 9x - 4 = -x \\)\n\nFor the first sub-case:\n\\[ 9x - 4 = x \\implies 8x = 4 \\implies x = \\frac{1}{2}. \\]\nSince \\( x = \\frac{1}{2} \\geq \\frac{1}{3} \\), this is a valid solution.\n\nFor the second sub-case:\n\\[ 9x - 4 = -x \\implies 10x = 4 \\implies x = \\frac{2}{5}. \\]\nSince \\( x = \\frac{2}{5} \\geq \\frac{1}{3} \\), this is also a valid solution.\n\n### Case 2: \\( 3x - 1 < 0 \\) (i.e., \\( x < \\frac{1}{3} \\))\nIn this case, \\( |3x - 1| = -(3x - 1) = -3x + 1 \\), so:\n\\[ f(f(x)) = |3(-3x + 1) - 1| = |-9x + 3 - 1| = |-9x + 2| = |9x - 2|. \\]\nWe need to solve:\n\\[ |9x - 2| = x. \\]\nThis gives us two sub-cases:\n1. \\( 9x - 2 = x \\)\n2. \\( 9x - 2 = -x \\)\n\nFor the first sub-case:\n\\[ 9x - 2 = x \\implies 8x = 2 \\implies x = \\frac{1}{4}. \\]\nSince \\( x = \\frac{1}{4} < \\frac{1}{3} \\), this is a valid solution.\n\nFor the second sub-case:\n\\[ 9x - 2 = -x \\implies 10x = 2 \\implies x = \\frac{1}{5}. \\]\nSince \\( x = \\frac{1}{5} < \\frac{1}{3} \\), this is also a valid solution.\n\n### Conclusion\nThe solutions to the equation \\( f(f(x)) = x \\) are \\( x = \\frac{1}{4}, \\frac{1}{5}, \\frac{2}{5}, \\frac{1}{2} \\). Therefore, the final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{\\frac{1}{5}, \\frac{1}{4}, \\frac{2}{5}, \\frac{1}{2}}. \\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{1}{5}, \\frac{1}{4}, \\frac{2}{5}, \\frac{1}{2}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"intermediate_algebra:564"}
